<title>SWITZERLAND: Tietmeyer says G10 sees calm currency markets.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says G10 sees calm currency markets.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said Group of 10 central bank governors believed world currency markets were calm and there was no reason for special concern.  </p>
<p>&quot;We see that the markets are relatively calm, not only inside Europe but also worldwide,&quot; Tietmeyer told reporters after the G10 central bankers' monthly meeting in Basle.</p>
<p>&quot;There is in our view for the time being no reason for special concern,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>He was speaking in his capacity as chairman of the G10 central bank governors.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
